    "name": "Euphrates Railway (Aleppo-Deir ez-Zor-Qamishli)",
    "name_arabic": "خط الفرات",
    "countries": "Syria",
    "gauge_mm": 1435,
    "year_opened": 1968,
    "era": "historic",
    "color": "#b45309",
    "corridor_confidence": "medium",
    "description": "Soviet-built Euphrates/Jazira corridor to the Turkish border",
    "notes": "Standard-gauge CFS line up the Euphrates and across the Jazira to the Turkish border at Qamishli.  [established] Built in stages with Soviet assistance: Aleppo-Al-Tabqah 1968, Al-Tabqah-Raqqa 1972, Raqqa-Deir ez-Zor 1973, Deir ez-Zor-Qamishli 1976.  [connections] Qamishli sits on the Turkish border opposite Nusaybin (on the Baghdad Railway) - a second Syria-Turkey rail touchpoint.",
    "history": "A standard-gauge (1,435 mm) line built 1968-1976 with Soviet monetary and industrial assistance, running from Aleppo along the Euphrates (Al-Thawra/Tabqa, Raqqa, Deir ez-Zor) and across the Jazira to Hasakah and Qamishli on the Turkish frontier.",
    "verification_status": "unverified",
